{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"**CORRECTION — withdraw the \"13th rename\" and \"5 fixtures, not 4\" claims in my earlier comment on this ticket. The plan's 12 is right, and so was ADVI4's 4.**\n\nRe-measured at `ce5795c6a5c` with a comment-insensitive AST comparison (`ast.parse(ast.unparse(node))` then `ast.dump`, which is what \"differing bodies\" has to mean, since comments are not AST nodes):\n\n- 39 paired twins directly under `tests/unit/`, 14 unpaired (S5's) — unchanged, still exact.\n- **78 identical shared definitions; 13 differing.** One of the 13 is the carved-out `test_unreadable_optional_config_warns_structurally_and_returns_false` in the whole-file-deletion pair, leaving **12 helper/fixture/class renames — exactly the 12 the Approach enumerates.**\n\nThe earlier claim that `store` in `tests/unit/test_identity_ts2_09f9.py` was a missing 13th rename was wrong. Its two copies differ **only in where a comment sits**:\n\n- base `:28-29` — `# Keep events unfolded so keyring events stay inspectable.` on its own line above `monkeypatch.setenv(\"REBAR_COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS\", \"9\" * 18)`\n- held-out `:33` — the same statement with a trailing `# keep events unfolded`\n\nIdentical code. It is a **dedupe** (keep the base copy), not a rename. My earlier comparison was comment-sensitive, so it reported a difference that does not exist at the AST level.\n\nThe fixture count follows from the same error. There are indeed **5** `@pytest.fixture` definitions shared across these pairs — `clean_registry` (test_attest_registry.py) and `store` in test_audit_serve.py, test_identity_3183.py, test_identity_4e9d.py and test_identity_ts2_09f9.py — but only **4 are renamed**, because the fifth is the identical one just described. ADVI4's 4 counted the renamed set and was correct.\n\nBy contrast `_head` in the same pair **is** a genuine rename and is correctly in the 12: the held-out copy drops the base's docstring, and a docstring is an `Expr`/`Constant` node, so the bodies really do differ.\n\n**What survives from that comment, and still governs the implementation:** the caller map and its two ordering constraints are unaffected, because they concern the 4 renamed fixtures and the helpers in the ts2_09f9 held-out module. Fixtures have **zero call-expression sites**, so a rename driven by call sites alone reports success while changing nothing — the bindings to repoint are **parameter names**. In `test_identity_ts2_09f9_heldout.py` the helper **signatures** `_tracker(store)` `:59`, `_head(store)` `:63`, `_ticket_dir(store)` `:81` and `_batched_keyadd_and_event(...)` `:193` take `store` as a parameter; since `store` there is deduped rather than renamed, those signatures keep their name, and only `_head` is renamed in that file. AC2's per-file `pytest --collect-only -q` counts remain the check that catches a missed binding, because a stale fixture parameter name is a collection-time fixture-not-found error."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793482395292626001,"uuid":"27777d19-bc86-43eb-9579-93392981d3f3"}